  "prompts": {
    "EXPLAIN_INSTRUCTION": "Explain in 2-4 sentences, for a test engineer, what this test checks, why it matters for the requirement, and what outcome is expected. Do not invent byte values.",
    "PARSE_INSTRUCTION": "Extract the UDS identifiers that requirement_text mentions or clearly implies, using only keys from spec_index. services must never be empty: always name the service whose behaviour the requirement specifies. Do not add DIDs, routines or services the text does not refer to.\nPhrase -> identifier guide:\n- read/report a value -> 0x22; write/set/store/change a value or calibration -> 0x2E\n- switch/enter/return to a session or mode -> 0x10\n- default session -> session 0x01; programming/flash/bootloader -> session 0x02; extended/diagnostic mode -> session 0x03\n- unlock, seed/key, security access -> 0x27; 'security level 1' -> level 0x01; programming-level unlock -> level 0x03\n- ECU reset/reboot -> 0x11; keep-alive/tester present -> 0x3E\n- start/stop/results of a routine or self-test -> 0x31 plus the routine id\n- read fault memory/trouble codes -> 0x19; clear them -> 0x14\n- DIDs and routines: match the words of the text to the names in spec_index (e.g. 'door actuator calibration' -> routine 0x0202 door_actuator_calibration, 'ambient colour' -> DID 0x0101 ambient_lighting_color_index). A stored setting is a DID; something started/stopped/run is a routine. List a DID only if the text names that value; 0xF186 is only for reading the current session.\nAdd 0x10 to services only when entering a session is a condition of the behaviour ('shall require extended session', 'only in the flash session') or the session switch itself is tested. 'In any/every session' is not a condition: fill sessions, do not add 0x10. Add 0x27 and a security level only if the text mentions unlocking, security access, seed/key or a security level. Fill sessions whenever sessions are named or implied.",
    "PLAN_INSTRUCTION": "Choose test cases that verify the requirement thoroughly: positive behaviour plus negative, session, security and timing checks where relevant. Each choice is a template_id from the catalog and an option_index from that template's options, with a one-sentence rationale. Do not repeat choices listed under rejected or already_kept.",
    "SCHEMA_RETRY_INSTRUCTION": "Your previous reply was not valid JSON for the required schema. Error: {error}\nReply again with only a JSON object that matches the schema.",
    "SYSTEM_PROMPT": "You are a UDS (ISO 14229) diagnostics test-planning assistant for an automotive ECU. You never write request or response bytes. You only reference identifiers that exist in the provided spec index, choose template ids and option indices from the provided catalog, and write short plain-English prose. Answer with JSON matching the schema when one is required."
  },
